  "notes": "{覚|さ}める means to wake up (from sleep) or to come to one's senses.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {覚|さ}ます (transitive, to wake someone)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{目|め}が{覚|さ}めている means \"is awake\" (state), not \"is waking up.\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {目|め}が{覚|さ}める: to wake up\n- {夢|ゆめ}から{覚|さ}める: to wake from a dream\n- {酔|よ}いが{覚|さ}める: to sober up\n- {恋|こい}から{覚|さ}める: to fall out of love\n\nHOMOPHONE (different kanji):\n- {覚|さ}める: to wake up, to sober up\n- {冷|さ}める: to cool down (temperature)\n\nBoth have the same transitivity pair pattern with {覚|さ}ます and {冷|さ}ます.",
